  "question": {
    "text": "Calcium lactate is a salt of weak acid i.e., lactic acid having general formula <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> . Aqueous solution of salt has 0.3 M concentration. pOH of solution is 5.60. If 90% of the salt is dissociated then what will be the value of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow></msub></math> ?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
